    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d211-a1">

                <pb facs="0271" n="221" sameAs="frus:frus1894/pg221"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure 1 in No.
                    180.—Translation.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Hanotaux to Mr. Eustis.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Paris</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1894-06-25T01:55:00+00:09"><hi rendition="#italic">June 25—1:55
                                a.m.</hi></date></dateline></opener>
                <p>It is with profound sorrow that I convey to your knowledge that the President of
                    the Republic has just died at Lyons from the effects of an attempt against his
                    life.</p>
                <p>The assassin was immediately arrested.</p>
                <p>I did not fail to direct, by telegraph, the representatives of France abroad to
                    convey this fatal news to the knowledge of the governments to which they are
                    accredited.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">G. Hanotaux.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
